ope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\\,\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant." 13194139537062 17592186576411 true] [17592186172648 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = xy^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537062 17592186576411 true] [17592186172648 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = xy^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139537062 17592186576411 false] [17592186172649 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+1)^{2}(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537062 17592186576411 true] [17592186172649 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+1)^{2}(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139537062 17592186576411 false] [17592186172649 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{2}(y-2).$ Th